INT. OFFICE - OPEN-PLAN FLOOR - MORNING

Cubicles. Motivational posters ("SYNERGY IS A VERB"). A glass conference room in the corner with a big screen blinking: ALL-HANDS 9:00.

KENDRA (30s, sleek blazer, lanyard) leans on a cubicle wall sipping oat-milk coffee. BARRY (40s, cargo shorts, laminated badge, thermos) sits at his desk, typing like it's a chore. LEILANI (20s, intern, bright tote bag) hugs a stack of binders. SCOTT (40s, manager, quarter-zip, headset) paces with his hands behind his back. DR. PRAKASH (50s, consultant, tweed jacket, tablet) stands quietly by the conference room.

SCOTT
Good morning, team! Beautiful day to be productive!

KENDRA
Morning, Scott.

BARRY
(muttering)
Morning.

LEILANI
Good morning, Mr. Scott!

SCOTT
Leilani, it's just Scott.

LEILANI
Sorry, Mr. Just Scott.

Kendra snorts coffee. Barry stifles a laugh.

SCOTT
Alright, alright. Dr. Prakash is here to help us transition into the exciting new Q3 optimization.

PRAKASH
Good morning.

KENDRA
Is it an audit?

SCOTT
It's a transition.

BARRY
Is it layoffs?

SCOTT
It's an opportunity!

LEILANI
Oh, I love opportunities.

PRAKASH
Perhaps we begin in the conference room.

SCOTT
Great idea, Dr. P.

BARRY
Hey, Kendra.

KENDRA
Yeah?

BARRY
Do you have the Henderson file?

KENDRA
You asked me yesterday.

BARRY
Right. But do you have it?

KENDRA
It's in the shared drive.

LEILANI
I have a binder on Henderson!

^SCOTT
We don't need the Henderson file today.

PRAKASH
Henderson is already resolved.

KENDRA
Wait, what?

They all stop. Prakash taps his tablet. The conference screen flickers, flashing a list of names. Under HENDERSON, a line: TERMINATED.

BARRY
Terminated? He's on vacation.

PRAKASH
He was. Henderson, Pruitt, Salazar, and Okoye.

SCOTT
Dr. Prakash, we agreed to sequence the announcement.

PRAKASH
I'm sequencing it now.

KENDRA
(low)
Barry, check your email.

Barry opens a window. His eyes go wide. Kendra grabs her phone. Leilani drops two binders.

LEILANI
Is it bad?

SCOTT
(brightly)
It's an opportunity!

Everyone looks at him. He laughs, weakly, and tugs the zipper of his quarter-zip all the way up.

KENDRA
Scott. Your name is on the list.

SCOTT
(a long beat)
Is it?

BARRY
Number one.

Scott looks at the screen. He doesn't breathe. Then, very slowly, he reaches for Barry's thermos and takes a long drink.

SCOTT
This coffee is terrible.

BARRY
It's tea.
